{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git diff edcf5f28ca775b32d3ec1ee3dc078ad27ba86887 8aedb0507390f3c7764182f7c05f647708a671d9 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go .pose/adr .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md b/.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md\nindex 10dd1225..1ed86f03 100644\n--- a/.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md\n+++ b/.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md\n@@ -80,3 +80,31 @@ Version and explicitly adopt new semantics. Historic bundles keep their sealed\n contract. Preview migration without rewriting evidence. A program may remain\n blocked after implementations finish; diagnostics must name the unmet criterion\n and its owner. Engine acceptance uses generic fixtures, not consumer adoption.\n+\n+## Amendment — 2026-11-16: a closed scope stands over a moved trust pin\n+\n+Spec `pose-closed-scope-stands-over-a-moved-federated-pin`. A dependency of\n+another project is accepted at the whole-repository revision the consumer's\n+trust pin names. Spec `pose-closeout-judges-the-manifest` (2026-11-01) made\n+closeout agree with `review verify`: any difference between a closed scope's\n+sealed manifest and the current one unapproves it. So every move of a pin\n+unapproved every closed scope that depends on that project. After harne8\n+pinned pose-dist at `edcf5f2`, 18 of its closed specs lost their approval.\n+The three dependencies of one of them had only had follow-up dispositions\n+recorded and been reviewed again.\n+\n+A closed scope's approval now stands over such a dependency when it is still\n+the commitment the reviewer accepted:\n+\n+- the same reference, identity and relationships;\n+- resolved and done, then and now;\n+- the same plan digest and governing contracts;\n+- a current review bundle;\n+- no blocker of the current manifest naming it.\n+\n+The current acceptance already requires current trust and an approved\n+review of the dependency. Its revision, content, evidence, implementation\n+digest and review may move with the pin. The trust policy digest, which holds\n+the pins, follows only when at least one dependency of another project moved\n+and was judged this way; a trust policy change alone still unapproves. A\n+same-project dependency keeps the rule it had.\ndiff --git a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\nindex 4ba04fe2..3f510f23 100644\n--- a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n+++ b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n@@ -2412,6 +2412,13 @@\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"closed-scope-stands-over-a-moved-federated-pin-integration\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/pose\", \"-run\", \"TestAClosedScopeStandsOverAMovedFederatedPin|TestAMovedFederatedPinThatChangesTheCommitmentStales|TestATrustPolicyChangeAloneStales\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n+        },\n         {\n           \"name\": \"federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\",\n           \"program\": \"go\",\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\nindex 0623571a..e30e2009 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ import (\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"slices\"\n \t\"sort\"\n \t\"strconv\"\n \t\"strings\"\n@@ -4653,12 +4654,29 @@ func (s Store) manifestStandsOver(sealed, current *FederatedRoadmapManifest) boo\n \t}\n \twas.Dependencies = append([]FederatedDependency{}, sealed.Dependencies...)\n \tmet := map[string]bool{}\n+\tpinMoved := false\n \tfor i := range was.Dependencies {\n \t\tthen, now := &was.Dependencies[i], current.Dependencies[i]\n \t\tif then.SourceRevision == now.SourceRevision && then.SourceDigest == now.SourceDigest && then.Status == now.Status {\n \t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t}\n-\t\tif now.Identity.Project != was.Coordinator.Project || then.Status != now.Status && now.Status != \"done\" {\n+\t\t// A dependency of another project is accepted at the revision the\n+\t\t// trust pin names, so moving the pin moves every such dependency. It\n+\t\t// stands when it is still the commitment the reviewer accepted: the\n+\t\t// same artifact and relationship, done, with the same plan and\n+\t\t// governing contracts, and accepted by the current manifest with no\n+\t\t// blocker naming it, which already requires current trust and a\n+\t\t// current approved review of it (spec\n+\t\t// pose-closed-scope-stands-over-a-moved-federated-pin).\n+\t\tif now.Identity.Project != was.Coordinator.Project {\n+\t\t\tif !externalDependencyStands(*then, now, current.Blockers) {\n+\t\t\t\treturn false\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t*then = now\n+\t\t\tpinMoved = true\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif then.Status != now.Status && now.Status != \"done\" {\n \t\t\treturn false\n \t\t}\n \t\tif !s.sameRoadmapApartFromLifecycle(now.Identity, then.SourceRevision, now.SourceRevision) {\n@@ -4675,10 +4693,43 @@ func (s Store) manifestStandsOver(sealed, current *FederatedRoadmapManifest) boo\n \t\t\tblockers = append(blockers, blocker)\n \t\t}\n \t}\n+\tif pinMoved {\n+\t\t// The trust policy holds the pins; a moved pin changes its digest.\n+\t\t// Every dependency of another project was judged above under the\n+\t\t// current policy, so its digest follows them.\n+\t\twas.TrustPolicyDigest = current.TrustPolicyDigest\n+\t}\n \twas.Blockers, was.Ready, was.Digest = blockers, current.Ready, current.Digest\n \treturn sameFederatedManifest(&was, current)\n }\n \n+// externalDependencyStands reports whether a dependency of another project,\n+// accepted at a moved pin, is still the commitment a closed scope's reviewer\n+// accepted. Its revision, content, evidence and review may have moved with\n+// the pin; its identity, relationship, resolution, done status, plan and\n+// governing contracts may not, and the current manifest names no blocker of\n+// it.\n+func externalDependencyStands(then, now FederatedDependency, currentBlockers []string) bool {\n+\tif then.Ref != now.Ref || then.Identity != now.Identity || then.Relationship != now.Relationship || !slices.Equal(then.Relationships, now.Relationships) {\n+\t\treturn false\n+\t}\n+\tif then.ResolutionState != \"resolved\" || now.ResolutionState != \"resolved\" || then.Status != \"done\" || now.Status != \"done\" {\n+\t\treturn false\n+\t}\n+\tif then.PlanDigest == \"\" || then.PlanDigest != now.PlanDigest || !slices.Equal(then.GoverningContracts, now.GoverningContracts) {\n+\t\treturn false\n+\t}\n+\tif now.ReviewBundleID == \"\" || now.ReviewBundleDigest == \"\" {\n+\t\treturn false\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, blocker := range currentBlockers {\n+\t\tif blocker == now.Ref || strings.HasPrefix(blocker, now.Ref+\":\") {\n+\t\t\treturn false\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn true\n+}\n+\n // sameRoadmapApartFromLifecycle reports whether a roadmap's committed file holds\n // the same between two revisions, but for its transition to done.\n func (s Store) sameRoadmapApartFromLifecycle(identity ArtifactRef, from, to string) bool {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
