{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '612,650p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go; sed -n '295,320p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go | sed -n '4705,4732p'; rg -n 'stand|manifest' pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_judges_manifest_test.go; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"\tprojection := ReviewBundleScope{Ref: scope.String(), Kind: scope.Kind, Slug: scope.Slug, Roadmap: scope.Roadmap, Milestone: scope.Milestone, Sections: []ReviewBundleInput{}}\n\texcluded := []ReviewBundleInput{}\n\tswitch scope.Kind {\n\tcase \"spec\":\n\t\tsp, err := s.GetSpec(scope.Slug)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn projection, nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tprojection.DependsOn = append([]string{}, sp.DependsOn...)\n\t\tif err := s.ValidateRemediationLineage(*sp); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn projection, nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tprojection.Remediates = append([]string{}, sp.Remediates...)\n\t\tsort.Strings(projection.Remediates)\n\t\tprojection.Supersedes = sp.Supersedes\n\t\tprojection.Components = append([]string{}, sp.Components...)\n\t\tprojection.Deliveries = append([]string{}, sp.Delivers...)\n\t\tsort.Strings(projection.DependsOn)\n\t\tsort.Strings(projection.Components)\n\t\tsort.Strings(projection.Deliveries)\n\t\tsections := markdownLevelTwoSections(sp.Body)\n\t\tfor _, name := range []string{\"intent\", \"requirements\", \"technical plan\", \"decisions\"} {\n\t\t\tbody := sections[name]\n\t\t\tif body == \"\" {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tprojection.Sections = append(projection.Sections, ReviewBundleInput{Kind: \"semantic-section\", Path: name, Digest: digestText(body), Reason: \"governed semantic review input\"})\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, name := range []string{\"tasks\", \"validation\", \"final report\"} {\n\t\t\tif sections[name] != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\texcluded = append(excluded, ReviewBundleInput{Kind: \"derived-section\", Path: name, Digest: digestText(sections[name]), Reason: \"operational closeout content is verified by its own gate\"})\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tlifecyclePath, err := filepath.Rel(s.Root, sp.Path)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn projection, nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\texcluded = append(excluded, ReviewBundleInput{Kind: \"lifecycle\", Path: filepath.ToSlash(lifecyclePath), Reason: \"status and completed_at do not define the reviewed semantic subject\"})\n\tcase \"milestone\":\n\t\t\treturn true, true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false, true\n}\n\n// governingContractsAtSeal is every contract this engine knows. A bundle sealed\n// now is held to all of them; one sealed by an engine that did not know a\n// contract never lists it, and is never retroactively held to it. That is the\n// property the adoption date could not have, because a date can be edited after\n// the fact and this cannot.\nfunc governingContractsAtSeal() []string {\n\tids := []string{}\n\tfor _, contract := range ReviewContracts() {\n\t\tids = append(ids, contract.ID)\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(ids)\n\treturn ids\n}\n\ntype ReviewBundle struct {\n\tSchemaVersion  int                 `json:\"schema_version\"`\n\tBundleID       string              `json:\"bundle_id\"`\n\tBundleDigest   string              `json:\"bundle_digest\"`\n\tState          string              `json:\"state\"`\n\tSealedAt       string              `json:\"sealed_at,omitempty\"`\n  4705\t\n  4706\t// externalDependencyStands reports whether a dependency of another project,\n  4707\t// accepted at a moved pin, is still the commitment a closed scope's reviewer\n  4708\t// accepted. Its revision, content, evidence and review may have moved with\n  4709\t// the pin; its identity, relationship, resolution, done status, plan and\n  4710\t// governing contracts may not, and the current manifest names no blocker of\n  4711\t// it.\n  4712\tfunc externalDependencyStands(then, now FederatedDependency, currentBlockers []string) bool {\n  4713\t\tif then.Ref != now.Ref || then.Identity != now.Identity || then.Relationship != now.Relationship || !slices.Equal(then.Relationships, now.Relationships) {\n  4714\t\t\treturn false\n  4715\t\t}\n  4716\t\tif then.ResolutionState != \"resolved\" || now.ResolutionState != \"resolved\" || then.Status != \"done\" || now.Status != \"done\" {\n  4717\t\t\treturn false\n  4718\t\t}\n  4719\t\tif then.PlanDigest == \"\" || then.PlanDigest != now.PlanDigest || !slices.Equal(then.GoverningContracts, now.GoverningContracts) {\n  4720\t\t\treturn false\n  4721\t\t}\n  4722\t\tif now.ReviewBundleID == \"\" || now.ReviewBundleDigest == \"\" {\n  4723\t\t\treturn false\n  4724\t\t}\n  4725\t\tfor _, blocker := range currentBlockers {\n  4726\t\t\tif blocker == now.Ref || strings.HasPrefix(blocker, now.Ref+\":\") {\n  4727\t\t\t\treturn false\n  4728\t\t\t}\n  4729\t\t}\n  4730\t\treturn true\n  4731\t}\n  4732\t\n37:\tif !strings.Contains(strings.Join(eval.Blockers, \" \"), \"federated manifest of milestone:program/core changed\") {\n38:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the refusal does not name the manifest: %v\", eval.Blockers)\n70:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the approval did not stand before the revocation: %+v\", eval)\n84:\t\tt.Fatal(\"a store with no resolver judged a manifest it cannot resolve\")\n107:// The exemption is for scopes with no bundle: a legacy attempt does not stand in for a\n138:// A seal with no manifest has nothing to compare, whenever it was made: absence proves\n153:\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"the fixture sealed a manifest\")\n158:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a seal with no manifest stood against one: %+v\", eval)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"The focused tests pass. I found a gap in the “same commitment” check: `PlanDigest` hashes the review procedure, not the dependency’s requirements or decisions. A dependency can change its requirements, receive a new approval, and still retain the consumer’s old approval. I’m checking the surrounding gates and regression tests before finalizing that finding.\n"}}
